`data-page` value in the HTML and matches the API guard page by page.

### Tests

`tests/attendance_correction_test.php` covers the whole round trip: filing,
the validation refusals (future date, short reason, 90-day window), the
duplicate 409, the locked-date 409, the ignored client `employee_id`, the
portal's own-only listing, approve applying (create and update) with an
independent recomputation of the hours / late minutes including the 300-minute
boundary, reject requiring remarks and leaving attendance unchanged, the
double-approve 409, the role guards, the queue filters and pagination, and one
`audit_log` row per mutation. It restores every attendance row it touches and
prints a PASS/FAIL summary.

## Supervisor teams (008)

`Supervisor` is a **team lead**, not a third payroll role. A team is defined
structurally and only once - every employee whose `employees.supervisor_id`
points at that employee - so there is no teams table to fall out of step with
the guard:

| Column | Type | Meaning |
|--------|------|---------|
| `employees.supervisor_id` | `BIGINT NULL` | the employee's team lead. Self-referencing FK to `employees.employee_id`, `ON DELETE SET NULL`, indexed (`idx_employees_supervisor`). Deleting a supervisor releases their team members instead of failing. |
| `loans.recommended_by` | `BIGINT NULL` | `users.user_id` of the Supervisor who recommended the loan (no FK, exactly like `attendance_corrections.reviewed_by` / `overtime_records.approved_by`) |
| `loans.recommended_at` | `DATETIME NULL` | when the recommendation was recorded |
| `loans.recommendation_remarks` | `VARCHAR(500) NULL` | the Supervisor's advice, shown to the Approver |

The role set in `api/_bootstrap.php` is now:

```php
const MAKER_ROLES      = ["Payroll Officer"];
const CHECKER_ROLES    = ["Approver"];
const ADMIN_ROLES      = ["Administrator"];
const SUPERVISOR_ROLE  = "Supervisor";
const PAYROLL_ROLES    = ["Payroll Officer", "Approver"];               // maker + checker
const TEAM_QUEUE_ROLES = ["Payroll Officer", "Approver", "Supervisor"]; // + team lead
const ALL_ROLES        = ["Employee", "Payroll Officer", "Approver", "Supervisor", "Administrator"];
```

`PAYROLL_ROLES` is deliberately **unchanged**: it is the key that opens
salaries, payslips, payroll periods / runs, reports, the ledger and the
dashboard, so a Supervisor is refused with 403 on all of them. Adding
`Supervisor` to `ALL_ROLES` only makes the role assignable on the Users screen
(`users.html` dropdown + the `assets/js/users.js` role hint).

### The central team-scope helpers (`api/_bootstrap.php`)

| Function | Signature | Behaviour |
|----------|-----------|-----------|
| `isSupervisor` | `(): bool` | true when the acting user's role is `Supervisor` |
| `currentEmployeeId` | `(): ?int` | the acting user's `employee_id`, `NULL` for a staff account with no employee link |
| `supervisorTeamIds` | `(PDO $pdo, int $supervisorEmployeeId): array` | employee ids whose `supervisor_id` is that employee. Never includes the supervisor. A non-positive id yields `[]` |
| `supervisorScopeIds` | `(PDO $pdo): ?array` | the GET filter: `null` = not a Supervisor (full queue), `[]` = a Supervisor who leads nobody (empty list), `int[]` = their team |
| `assertSupervises` | `(PDO $pdo, int $employeeId, string $what): void` | 403 unless the actor is a Supervisor **and** their account has an employee link **and** the target is not themselves **and** the target's `supervisor_id` is that Supervisor |
| `assertTeamReadScope` | `(PDO $pdo, int $employeeId, string $what): void` | the read-side twin: a no-op for the maker / checker, 403 for a Supervisor asking about an employee outside their team |

Refusal messages are explicit, because these are the three mistakes a team lead
actually makes:

* own request -> `You cannot <what> because it is your own request. A
  Supervisor may never approve, reject or recommend their own request -
  another reviewer must decide it.`
* another team -> `Employee #N is not in your team, so you cannot <what>.
  A Supervisor may only decide their own team's requests.`
* no employee link -> `This Supervisor account is not linked to an employee
  record, so it leads no team and cannot <what>.`

A Supervisor user with **no** `employee_id` therefore supervises nobody: every
guard answers 403 (never a PHP error or a 500), and every list comes back empty
with `success: true`.

### Per-endpoint behaviour

| Endpoint | Maker / Checker | Supervisor |
|----------|-----------------|------------|
| `GET attendance.php` | full view | **200**, team only. `?date=` / `?summary=` filtered; `?id=` / `?employee_detail=` for a non-team employee -> 403 |
| `POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE attendance.php` | maker only | **403** (mutations stay maker-only) |
| `GET attendance_corrections.php` | full queue | **200**, team only (a filter, not a 403) |
| `PATCH attendance_corrections.php` | maker decides | **200** for a team member; 403 for another team / own request / no employee link |
| `GET overtime_records.php` | full queue | **200**, team only (all five query shapes) |
| `PATCH overtime_records.php` | maker decides | **200** for a team member; 403 otherwise |
| `POST/PUT/DELETE overtime_records.php` | maker only | **403** |
| `GET leave_requests.php` | every request | **200**, team only |
| `PATCH leave_requests.php` | maker decides | **200** for a team member; 403 otherwise |
| `POST/PUT/DELETE leave_requests.php` | maker only | **403** |
| `GET loans.php` | every loan | **200**, team only (carries `recommended_by` / `has_recommendation`) |
| `PATCH loans.php action=recommend` | **403** (no recommendation step) | **200** for a team member. Records `recommended_by` / `recommended_at` / `recommendation_remarks` and **never** changes `loans.status` |
| `PATCH loans.php action=approve` | Approver only | **403** - a Supervisor can never decide a loan |
| `POST/PUT/DELETE loans.php`, `PATCH loans.php status` | maker only | **403** |
| `employees` / `salary_rates` / `dashboard` / `reports` / `payslips` / `payroll_runs` / `payroll_periods` / `ledger` / `allowances` / `deductions` / `cash_disbursements` / `departments` / `positions` / `qr_codes` / `leave_types` / `leave_balances` | unchanged | **403** - no salaries, no payroll editing |
| `users.php` / `audit_log.php` | Administrator | **403** |
| `auth.php`, `scan_attendance.php` | open | **open** |

`auth.php?action=verify` (kiosk exit) was **not** extended: it is a technical
operation this file has always kept to Administrator plus the two payroll
roles, and changing authentication was out of scope for this step. A Supervisor
can still use the kiosk itself, but authorising a kiosk exit answers 403.

### Nav (`assets/js/nav.js`)

The `NAV_ACCESS` rows that gained `Supervisor` are exactly the team screens:

```
attendance.html              ["Payroll Officer", "Approver", "Supervisor"]
leave.html                   ["Payroll Officer", "Approver", "Supervisor"]
overtime.html                ["Payroll Officer", "Approver", "Supervisor"]
attendance_corrections.html  ["Payroll Officer", "Approver", "Supervisor"]
loans.html                   ["Payroll Officer", "Approver", "Supervisor"]
kiosk.html                   ["Employee", "Payroll Officer", "Approver", "Supervisor", "Administrator"]
```

Dashboard, Employees, Salary Rates, Payroll Periods / Runs, Payslips, Reports,
Users and Audit Log are untouched, so a Supervisor does not see them at all.
The default-hidden `nav-locked` behaviour and every `data-page` value are
unchanged. `assets/js/attendance_corrections.js` and `assets/js/loans.js` render
their decision buttons for a Supervisor too (the API is still the real guard),
and `assets/js/loans.js` hides the add-loan form from them.

### Tests

`tests/supervisor_scope_test.php` proves the whole role on real fixtures (two
teams, a Supervisor with no employee link, a maker and a checker): team-scoped
GET lists, team decisions returning 200, another team's request -> 403, the
own-request rule -> 403, the unlinked Supervisor -> 403 everywhere, a loan
recommendation that leaves `status` untouched, a refused loan approval, the
closed salary / payroll screens, the maker regression, and one `audit_log` row
per decision. It removes every fixture it creates and asserts employees 4, 5
and 8 are unchanged.

`tests/role_matrix_test.php` and `tests/nav_matrix_test.php` carry the
`Supervisor` column / row for every page and endpoint they cover.

